---
export const prerender = false;
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '~/components/Footer.astro';
import ProjectUpdates from '~/components/ProjectUpdates.astro';
import { websiteFeed } from '~/lib/publication/website';
import '~/styles/project-journal.css';
const feed = await websiteFeed(Astro.locals.runtime.env, 'threadline');
Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'no-store');
---
<BaseLayout title="Threadline · Project journal · Kazon Wilson" description="Helping developers pick up the thread of their work. Follow Threadline from its first prototype to the latest milestone.">
  <div class="project-shell"><nav class="project-nav" aria-label="Project navigation"><a href="/">Kazon Wilson</a><a href="/building">All projects</a></nav>
    <header class="project-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Project journal · Development</p><h1>Threadline</h1><p class="lead">Pick up where you left off.</p><p>Switching tasks can mean reconstructing what you were doing. I’m building a way to keep related work together inside the code editor.</p><p class="project-note">An internal prototype. The milestones below distinguish plans, built pieces, checks and availability.</p><p class="intended-experience"><strong>The intended experience:</strong> Work on a task, handle an interruption, then return to its related code and context. Threadline should help keep that work together, with you able to correct its suggestions.</p></header>
    <ProjectUpdates feed={feed} projectId="threadline" />
  </div><Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
